-- readme --
# FSP Talent Platform — autonomous Codex bootstrap

Стартовый репозиторий для автономной разработки цифровой платформы подбора ИТ-специалистов по ТЗ ФСП 2026.

## Уже подготовлено

- исходное ТЗ в `docs/source/`;
- формализованная матрица требований;
- продуктовая и техническая архитектура;
- дизайн-система по официальному брендбуку ФСП;
- концепция уникального calibrated assessment + anti-leak/anti-AI-by-design;
- ProofMatch / Evidence-Graph Reverse Matching + Talent Radar;
- employer hiring pipeline, post-match chat and CPU-local AI task-copilot design;
- conference Q&A clarifications from 2026-10-06 integrated into requirements;
- runnable skeleton `Next.js + FastAPI + PostgreSQL + Keycloak`;
- Docker Compose для локального/демо запуска без обязательного GPU;
- Playwright для E2E и скриншотов desktop/tablet/mobile;
- supervisor вокруг `codex exec`;
- recovery-loop: код → build → services → tests → logs → repair → retry;
- Telegram-репортинг статусов и скриншотов;
- Git checkpoint/push после успешной верификации;
- backlog/milestones и критерии `READY`.

## Главный принцип

Codex не может сам объявить работу проверенной. Статус `VERIFIED` выставляется только после реального
`docker compose build/up`, health checks, тестов и E2E внешним supervisor.

## Быстрый старт

1. Прочитай `docs/SETUP_SYNOLOGY_CODEX_RU.md`.
2. `cp .env.example .env`
3. `cp .env.agent.example .env.agent`
4. Заполни секреты локально.
5. Выполни:
   ```bash
   ./agent/doctor.sh
   ./agent/autopilot.sh
   ```

## Режимы

- Интерактивный Codex: см. `CODEX_START.md`.
- Полный автономный цикл: `./agent/autopilot.sh`.
- Только верификация: `./agent/verify.sh`.
- Скриншоты: `./agent/capture-screenshots.sh`.
- Telegram test: `./agent/telegram.sh message "FSP agent online"`.

## Что является готовым сейчас

Приложение содержит только рабочий bootstrap/smoke-каркас. Полная бизнес-функциональность намеренно
оставлена Codex: этот репозиторий — управляемая спецификация, среда разработки, контроль качества и
агентный контур.
-- compose --
services:
  app-db:
    image: postgres:17-alpine
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: ${POSTGRES_DB:-fsp}
      POSTGRES_USER: ${POSTGRES_USER:-fsp}
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}
    volumes:
      - app-db-data:/var/lib/postgresql/data
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "pg_isready -U ${POSTGRES_USER:-fsp} -d ${POSTGRES_DB:-fsp}"]
      interval: 5s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 20
    restart: unless-stopped

  keycloak-db:
    image: postgres:17-alpine
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: ${KEYCLOAK_DB:-keycloak}
      POSTGRES_USER: ${KEYCLOAK_DB_USER:-keycloak}
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${KEYCLOAK_DB_PASSWORD}
    volumes:
      - keycloak-db-data:/var/lib/postgresql/data
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "pg_isready -U ${KEYCLOAK_DB_USER:-keycloak} -d ${KEYCLOAK_DB:-keycloak}"]
      interval: 5s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 20
    restart: unless-stopped

  mailpit:
    image: axllent/mailpit:v1.27
    ports:
      - "${MAILPIT_PORT:-8025}:8025"
    restart: unless-stopped

  keycloak:
    image: quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.8.0
    command: ["start-dev", "--import-realm"]
    environment:
      KC_DB: postgres
      KC_DB_URL: jdbc:postgresql://keycloak-db:5432/${KEYCLOAK_DB:-keycloak}
      KC_DB_USERNAME: ${KEYCLOAK_DB_USER:-keycloak}
      KC_DB_PASSWORD: ${KEYCLOAK_DB_PASSWORD}
      KC_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_USERNAME: ${KEYCLOAK_ADMIN:-admin}
      KC_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD: ${KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD}
      KC_HEALTH_ENABLED: "true"
    volumes:
      - ./infrastructure/keycloak/realm-fsp.json:/opt/keycloak/data/import/realm-fsp.json:ro
    ports:
      - "${KEYCLOAK_PORT:-8081}:8080"
    depends_on:
      keycloak-db:
        condition: service_healthy
      mailpit:
        condition: service_started
    restart: unless-stopped

  backend:
    build:
      context: ./backend
    environment:
      APP_ENV: ${APP_ENV:-development}
      DATABASE_URL: ${DATABASE_URL}
      KEYCLOAK_INTERNAL_URL: ${KEYCLOAK_INTERNAL_URL:-http://keycloak:8080}
      KEYCLOAK_PUBLIC_URL: ${KEYCLOAK_PUBLIC_URL:-http://localhost:8081}
      KEYCLOAK_REALM: ${KEYCLOAK_REALM:-fsp}
      KEYCLOAK_ISSUER: ${KEYCLOAK_ISSUER:-http://localhost:8081/realms/fsp}
      KEYCLOAK_JWKS_URL: ${KEYCLOAK_JWKS_URL:-http://keycloak:8080/realms/fsp/protocol/openid-connect/certs}
      KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID: ${KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID:-fsp-web}
      CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS: ${CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS:-http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000}
      PRIVATE_STORAGE_DIR: ${PRIVATE_STORAGE_DIR:-/var/lib/fsp/private}
      PRIVACY_RETENTION_DAYS: ${PRIVACY_RETENTION_DAYS:-30}
      LOCAL_AI_ENABLED: ${LOCAL_AI_ENABLED:-false}
      LOCAL_AI_BASE_URL: ${LOCAL_AI_BASE_URL:-http://local-ai:11434}
      LOCAL_AI_MODEL: ${LOCAL_AI_MODEL:-}
      LOCAL_AI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS: ${LOCAL_AI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:-60}
      LOCAL_AI_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE: ${LOCAL_AI_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE:-5}
      LOCAL_AI_MAX_ACTIVE_JOBS_PER_COMPANY: ${LOCAL_AI_MAX_ACTIVE_JOBS_PER_COMPANY:-1}
    volumes:
      - backend-private-data:/var/lib/fsp/private
      # The offline validation contract compares the generated report with
      # the committed artifact while tests run inside the backend container.
      - ./docs/VALIDATION_RESULTS.json:/app/docs/VALIDATION_RESULTS.json:ro
    ports:
      - "${BACKEND_PORT:-8000}:8000"
    depends_on:
      app-db:
        condition: service_healthy
      keycloak:
        condition: service_started
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "python", "-c", "import urllib.request; urllib.request.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:8000/health/ready', timeout=3)"]
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 20
    restart: unless-stopped

  # Optional CPU-only local model runtime. Core services deliberately do not
  # depend on this profile so AI-off startup remains the default path.
  local-ai:
    image: ${LOCAL_AI_IMAGE:-ollama/ollama:0.40.0}
    profiles: ["local-ai"]
    environment:
      OLLAMA_HOST: 0.0.0.0:11434
      OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL: "1"
      OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS: "1"
      OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE: ${LOCAL_AI_KEEP_ALIVE:-5m}
    volumes:
      - local-ai-data:/root/.ollama
    ports:
      - "${LOCAL_AI_PORT:-11434}:11434"
    cpus: ${LOCAL_AI_CPU_LIMIT:-4.0}
    mem_limit: ${LOCAL_AI_MEMORY_LIMIT:-8g}
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "OLLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1:11434 ollama list >/dev/null 2>&1"]
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 12
    restart: unless-stopped

  frontend:
    build:
      context: ./frontend
    environment:
      NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL: ${NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL:-http://localhost:8000}
      NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYCLOAK_URL: ${NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYCLOAK_URL:-http://localhost:8081}
      NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYCLOAK_REALM: ${NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYCLOAK_REALM:-fsp}
      NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID: ${NEXT_PUBLIC_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID:-fsp-web}
    ports:
      - "${FRONTEND_PORT:-3000}:3000"
    depends_on:
      backend:
        condition: service_healthy
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD", "node", "-e", "fetch('http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/health').then(r=>{if(!r.ok)process.exit(1)}).catch(()=>process.exit(1))"]
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 20
    restart: unless-stopped

  qa:
    profiles: ["test"]
    build:
      context: ./qa
    environment:
      FRONTEND_BASE_URL: http://frontend:3000
      BACKEND_BASE_URL: http://backend:8000
      AUTH_E2E_ENABLED: "true"
      KEYCLOAK_E2E_BASE_URL: http://keycloak:8080
      KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_USERNAME: ${KEYCLOAK_ADMIN:-admin}
      KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD: ${KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD}
      MAILPIT_BASE_URL: http://mailpit:8025
      SCREENSHOT_OUTPUT: /workspace/screenshots
    volumes:
      - ./.agent/screenshots/latest:/workspace/screenshots
    depends_on:
      frontend:
        condition: service_healthy
      backend:
        condition: service_healthy

volumes:
  app-db-data:
  keycloak-db-data:
  backend-private-data:
  local-ai-data:
-- demo reset --
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -Eeuo pipefail
root="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)"
cd "$root"

if [[ "${DEMO_RESET_CONFIRM:-}" != "YES" ]]; then
  read -r -p "This destroys FSP compose demo database volumes. Type RESET-FSP-DEMO: " ans
  [[ "$ans" == "RESET-FSP-DEMO" ]] || { echo "cancelled"; exit 1; }
fi

docker compose down -v
docker compose up -d --build
"$root/agent/wait-http.sh" "${BACKEND_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:8000}/health" 240
"$root/agent/wait-http.sh" "${FRONTEND_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:3000}/api/health" 240

docker compose exec -T backend python -m app.seed_demo
-- presentation --
# Pitch / presentation outline

1. Problem: keyword resumes and noisy generic job boards.
2. Product insight: reverse recruitment + verified evidence, not resume self-description.
3. Candidate journey and `.ru`/Keycloak identity flow.
4. Calibrated unique assessment: different forms, comparable difficulty, no grade-collapse.
5. Anti-leak / anti-AI-by-design: progressive verification, session-specific artifacts, advisory integrity signals.
6. Verified Skill Passport + synthetic FSP achievements as bounded positive evidence.
7. Talent Radar: employer starts from categories, not a flat resume board.
8. ProofMatch / Evidence-Graph Reverse Matching: score, confidence, reasons and gaps; unconfirmed grade remains visible.
9. Invitation with salary upfront → accepted MATCH → internal chat/contact unlock.
10. Employer Hiring Pipeline: extra employer-authored/graded stages; optional CPU-local task copilot using prior approved tasks.
11. 152-FZ-oriented privacy controls and minor-consent flow.
12. Validation: matching metrics vs keyword baseline + assessment confusion/stability/discrimination.
13. Load test on CPU-only target host; no GPU dependency.
14. Architecture / Keycloak / Docker / OpenAPI / local adapters.
15. Brand-responsive UI and Telegram autonomous-development evidence/screenshots.
16. Live demo.
17. Roadmap: real FSP registry/Keycloak integration, ATS, employer trust.

Keep the core 35% matching criterion and 25% assessment criterion central in the narrative.
